em* (in terms of linear transformations) states the following: \n\n $T$ is a bijection $\\,⟺\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Im}(T)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{rank}(T)=n \\\\  & \\text{Ker}(T)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{nullity}(T)=0\\end{aligned}$ \n$\\,⟺\\,$  $T$ is invertible\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459244 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124632 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eead7563-6231-5490-9a10-721d09133352" :knowledge-point/title "Recognizing Parts of the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c5c3d72-de8a-55bc-9aae-d88fff92e5c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458743} {:answer/id #uuid "757b0193-eb8e-5530-9a2d-8126646fe135" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458834} {:answer/id #uuid "99b33fe7-4038-5c19-b93d-909bc240d366" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458896} {:answer/id #uuid "e3098434-cc76-5102-98c2-96118c83bc3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{nullity}(T)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459024} {:answer/id #uuid "f5700bee-8420-5b66-ae88-ee3f003570e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459062}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "757b0193-eb8e-5530-9a2d-8126646fe135" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458834} :answer-field/id #uuid "bec51248-9b9b-569c-a543-cda111929d9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459168}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6acf0a48-db0b-58e8-8817-08a155161bed" :question/math-academy-id "q-141448" :question/problem "$T$ is a bijection $\\,⟺\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Im}(T)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{rank}(T)=\\bbox[3pt,white,border: 2px solid Gainsboro]{\\phantom{W}} \\\\  & \\text{Ker}(T)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{nullity}(T)=0\\end{aligned}$ \n$\\,⟺\\,$  $T$ is invertible\n\nConsider the equivalence above, where $T:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{n}$ is a linear transformation whose standard matrix is $T.$ Which of the following should be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the *invertible matrix theorem* (in terms of linear transformations) states the following: \n\n $T$ is a bijection $\\,⟺\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Im}(T)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{rank}(T)=n \\\\  & \\text{Ker}(T)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{nullity}(T)=0\\end{aligned}$ \n$\\,⟺\\,$  $T$ is invertible\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $n.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272284 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124632 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eead7563-6231-5490-9a10-721d09133352" :knowledge-point/title "Recognizing Parts of the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "079f5dae-bfcf-5b50-ba4b-ae83bc6f55b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{Im}(T)$ and $\\text{Ker}(T)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269339} {:answer/id #uuid "9d1d9335-bfdb-5b54-9538-0501d53fbad2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{Null}(T)$ and $\\text{Ker}(T)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270657} {:answer/id #uuid "abe72a0c-363a-5a3a-8cac-526a5e9222e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{Ker}(T)$ and $\\text{Domain}(T)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270803} {:answer/id #uuid "b6ee4548-b055-5785-a92c-1b