lity}(T)=0\\end{aligned}$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since $T(x)=v$ has no solution, we have that $v\\notin \\text{Im}(T),$ hence $\\text{Im}(T)\\ne {R}^{5}.$ According to the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{Im}(T)\\ne {R}^{5},$ the transformation $T$ and the matrix $T$ are not invertible.\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $T$ is not invertible, the invertible matrix theorem implies that  $\\text{Ker}(T)\\ne {0}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $T$ is not invertible, the invertible matrix theorem implies that $\\text{nullity}(T)\\ne 0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326728 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124521 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9d77214-796e-558f-a364-00ae3e25cc13" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3b6b69e-fdda-5b48-8cbe-b6154cd7c5d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450606} {:answer/id #uuid "97c3efcd-f3c2-540f-afcf-4d2de2e5f841" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450607}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97c3efcd-f3c2-540f-afcf-4d2de2e5f841" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450607} :answer-field/id #uuid "53da20ae-ae94-56fd-81c5-8688aef36c20" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451257} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bfca9365-98df-5eb7-95b1-2fb60431dc72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450608} {:answer/id #uuid "6fac619f-5615-571c-9063